---
// Result figure: mean score by system and reasoning effort, with what each
// configuration cost. Mirrors Figure 2 of the paper and reads the same export.
---

<figure class="ai4ai-scatter" data-ai4ai-bars>
  <div class="ai4ai-scatter-controls">
    <label class="ai4ai-control">
      <span>Task</span>
      <select data-task-filter aria-label="Filter by task"></select>
    </label>
    <p class="ai4ai-readout" data-readout>Loading…</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ai4ai-key">
    <span><i class="ai4ai-key-dash"></i>0.10 — the code already in the repository</span>
    <span><i class="ai4ai-key-ramp"></i>deeper colour = the agent was told to think harder</span>
  </div>

  <div class="ai4ai-plot" data-plot>
    <div class="ai4ai-tooltip" data-tooltip hidden></div>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    One group per model, one bar per reasoning-effort level, joined so the effort ladder is
    visible; deeper colour is more effort. Each bar is that configuration's mean score over the
    ten tasks, labelled with the score and with what its four hours of exploration cost. The
    dashed line at <strong>0.10</strong> is the algorithm each repository already ships. Pick a
    task to see the same configurations on that task alone.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  import "@/scripts/ai4ai-bars";
</script>
